# Cost & quota rules for this repo (follow strictly)

## Reading
- Never read a whole large file. Grep first, then read only the line range you need (±30 lines).
- Do not re-read a file you already read in this chat unless it changed.
- Do not scan docs/ broadly. Read only the doc the task names. Ignore docs/features/*_COMPLETE.md and *_SUMMARY.md (stale).
- Before creating anything, one grep for an existing equivalent (RULE 2) — not a full repo tour.

## Editing
- Make the smallest edit that solves the task. Use targeted edits, never rewrite a whole file.
- No refactors, renames, formatting or "improvements" outside the task.
- Do NOT create new .md files (summaries, reports, plans, *_COMPLETE.md). Update the one existing status table/doc for that feature, in 1–3 lines.
- No new folders. New files only inside Modules/{Name}/app/{Layer}/ and only if no existing file fits.

## Tests (the full suite takes 4–6 hours — never run it)
- Run ONLY the test files for what you changed:
  php vendor/bin/pest path/to/ThatTest.php   (or --filter=name)
- PHP is not on PATH: use C:\laragon\bin\php\php-8.3.30-Win32-vs16-x64\php.exe
- Run each test file once; if it passes, do not run it again. If it fails, fix and re-run only that file.
- If a failure is unrelated to your change, check with `git stash` once, report it in one line, do not fix it.
- Write tests only for the new behaviour (1 happy path + the main failure case). No duplicate test files.
- Sign-up/login changes: also run Modules/Authentication/tests/Feature/SignupCriticalPathTest.php (RULE 16).
- Never run migrate:fresh. Never run npm build unless asked.

## Git
- Default: work on **`main` only**. No feature/fix/chore side branches and no PRs unless the user explicitly asks for that named step.
- Commit / push / PR / merge each only when the user clearly asks in that turn. Never invent a PR after push.
- Do not run git log/diff on the whole history; limit with -n 5 or a path.
- Production deploys are **manual** (GitHub CI is unreliable) — give the user pull/migrate commands; do not assume auto-deploy.

## Process
- One task per chat. If the task is unclear, ask ONE question before starting, not after building.
- No long plans or explanations. Act, then report.
- Final reply: short, in Egyptian Arabic: what's done / what's left / what you need from me. No code dumps, no file-by-file lists.
- Stop when the task is done. Do not suggest or start extra work.
- Prefer cheaper / Auto model for trivial wraps, docs, config, commits. Never Max / Opus / strong models for housekeeping. Save strong models for architecture, money bugs, or hard debug only.

